 366:      +0x00/+0x08 (HIGH lane, 0 either way -- the entries-4/8 note above) are not.
 367: 
 368:      AND THE CONSEQUENCE, which is the finding rather than the correction:
 369:      *** `acc ctl0c' NEVER REDS UNDER ANY OF THE FIFTEEN LEGS OF TABLE 12 *** -- including
 370:      `G_clr_ctl4r', the equivalent-cell decline the PAIR was added to make observable.  That
 371:      mutant is `relative_addr == CRIME_CONTROL' (0x08); +0x0c is a DIFFERENT switch label.  Same
 372:      storage, different switch.  So the DISCRIMINATING half of the pair carries no measured kill.
 373:      Accept-row failability says a row is not discharged by EXISTING.  **Do NOT add a row -- the
 374:      rows already exist.**  Either run a decline that actually reaches 0x0c, or stop claiming
 375:      `ctl0c' as `G_lane_ctl''s channel.
 376:      *** DISCHARGED 2026-09-17 (ctl0c_discharge_20260917/, predictions written before the run): a decline
 377:      that reaches 0x0c, M_ctl0c_decline, reds exactly `acc ctl0c' and `p acc ctl0c' -- 202 of the then 204
 378:      rows -- and the base leg is green.  The pair's discriminating half carries a measured kill. ***
 379: 
 380: *** AND THE FACE THIS DETECTOR DID **NOT** CLOSE UNTIL REPAIR 15, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE A CONTRACT THAT
 381:     HIDES ITS HOLES IS WORSE THAN NONE. ***
 382:   THE DECLINE-SUPPRESSION FACE.  The `goto crime_declined' SKIPS the register switch, and what it skips is
 383:   an OMISSION -- it reads, writes and tests nothing -- so every floor clause in this project enumerates the
 384:   EMPTY SET over it.  Two mutants that condition the `goto' on a LABEL score 188/188 against this probe:  [188-row]
 385:       M3_timelatch   the goto moved inside the latch block, exempting CRIME_TIME  -- 188/188  [188-row]
 386:       M5_revlatch    the same at CRIME_REV                                        -- 188/188  [188-row]
 387:   with M4_timeplain (the same edit WITHOUT the latch conjunct) killed at 184/188 and M6_istlatch (the same  [188-row]
 388:   edit at INTSTAT) killed at 185/188 -- the controls that make those two escapes mean `no row looked'.  [188-row]
 389:   *** REPAIR 15 (2026-09-26) ROWS THE OPEN CELLS.  The floor, by the flagship's first-hand re-ruling
 390:   (artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md), is {observable skipped label} x
 391:   {latch SET}.  M3/M5 escaped because no refusal at TIME or REV with the latch already SET had a channel: the
 392:   `time' and `rev' sessions refuse there FIRST, and the `latch x5' session's later refusals at +0x00 and +0x38
 393:   run from CODE (REV's redirect needs the PROM window) with no TIME sample after them.  The `tl' and `rl' rows
 394:   refuse at +0x07 FIRST, then at the label.  The five guest-observable labels, the label-swap built for each,
 395:   and the table that measures it (scores are in those tables' logs, never here):
 396:       INTSTAT  M6_istlatch      istat sb/lh/sh                  repair14_20260916/ (table 12)
 397:       INTMASK  M7_intmasklatch  imask sb/lh/sh                  table13a_20260925/
 398:       CONTROL  M8_ctllatch      sb08 msg, sh08b run, gate run   table13a_20260925/
 399:       TIME     M3_timelatch     tl lb/sb/lh/sh                  table14_20260926/
 400:       REV      M5_revlatch      rl lb/lh/sb/sh pc               table14_20260926/
 401:   DOG (a bare `break;') and default (host log only -- and `mid nodflt' already reads it after a latch-
 402:   setting refusal: M1_gotolatch reddened it in table 12) have no guest-observable arm: clause (e).
 403:   ENTRIES 13 AND 17 of ACCEPTS (`sw'/`sd +0x08 = 0x0200', CONTROL's DOG mask): the arm clears DOG and nothing
 404:   prints, and the prelude re-forces the register at every access, so the CONTROL text COUNT is the cell's one
 405:   observable -- and no row read it in a session holding that write.  `ctldog sw msg'/`ctldog sd msg' are the pair
 406:   (D_nodogclear, the DOG branch's clear deleted; table14_20260926/).  A SILENT decline of the DOG-only write
 407:   changes nothing any access can see: EQUIVALENT, disclosed.
 408:   REPAIR 16 (2026-09-26) PINS THE CONTROL ARM'S RESIDUE-TEXT COUNT FOR EACH OF ITS THREE CLEARS IN BOTH LATCH
 409:   STATES.  FLOOR: the two TESTED bits' clears (DOG, HARD_RESET -- each masked as a case in the arm), in the
 410:   latch-CLEAR state where an accepted write's residue is the cell's only observable -- the CHANNEL conditional on
 411:   entries 13 and 17 (rerule_20260925/), extended by sibling parity to the arm's other tested bit
 412:   (repair15_pass2_20260926/fable5_r15p2.md): `ctldog sw/sd msg' (D_nodogclear), `ctlrst sw/sd msg' (H_noresetclear).
 413:   Everything else in this block is a STRENGTHENING above that floor, measured in table15a_20260926/ and
 414:   table16_20260926/.
 415:   THE LATCH IS NOT AN AXIS OF THIS ARM: the CONTROL arm reads no latch (`d->warned' has one reader and one writer,
 416:   both in the decline block), so a clear gated on it is clause (e) -- ROWED ANYWAY: `rearm ctl msg' (DOG, latch
 417:   SET; L_dogclr) and `rst 4w/8w msg' (HARD_RESET, latch SET; L_rstclr).
 418:   ENDIANESS (0x0100) is cleared unconditionally and never branched on: clause (e), NOT a member of the tested-bit
 419:   class.  Its clear skipped (E_noendianclear) is carried as a SIDE EFFECT of the ten-write aggregate counts, a
 420:   strengthening and not a floor claim.
 421:   `latch ctl msg' (CLEAR) and `rearm ctl msg' (SET) are AGGREGATE prefix counts over the ten accepted CONTROL
 422:   writes in ACCEPTS (every `rearm' entry runs latch SET: the refused `lb +0x07' precedes the loop).  They attribute
 423:   by count value only -- L_dogclr and an ENDIANESS-latch-SET skip both read 6 on `rearm'; W_ctl8w reads 2 -- and
 424:   the want of 4 encodes ACCEPTS' composition: any edit that adds or removes a printing CONTROL write moves it.
 425:   The count pins the NUMBER of texts, not their VALUE.  A clear skipped only when another bit of the written value
 426:   is set -- a floor cell crossed with one bit of the relationally compared residue (#549 D1) -- leaves every count
 427:   unchanged: MEASURED for DOG (D_dogbit0: the 0x0201 twin prints 0x201 where the fix prints 0x1); DERIVED, not
 428:   built, for HARD_RESET and ENDIANESS (every accepted reset store here is exactly 0x0800; both 0x0100 writes have
 429:   bit 0 clear).  Clause (e), disclosed as a family.  A value anchor BESIDE the prefix count would carry the DOG
 430:   instance at zero sessions (filed); an anchor IN PLACE of it loses H_noresetclear (the `ctlrst' twin 0x0001 carries
 431:   no HARD_RESET bit: repair16_f2_20260926/opus_f2/replay_ctl.out).
 432:   The count is read under single-stepping, where `debug()' and `fatal()' both print: the arm's `fatal()' demoted to
 433:   `debug()' (M_ctldebug) is invisible to every row here and visible to one free-running accepted `sw 0x0001'
 434:   (repair16_f2_20260926/opus_f2/disc_f2.out).  Disclosed; the free-running session is filed.
 435:   NOT ROWED, disclosed as clause (e), each measured by the Opus seat on repair 15's pass 2 (opus_r15p2_20260926/):
 436:   a latch-SET 2-byte CONTROL write with HARD_RESET clear (host text only; every latch-SET 2-byte write here carries
 437:   0x0800); at INTSTAT and INTMASK, the width x direction x latch-state joints no session reaches (1R with the latch
 438:   SET; 1W, 2R, 2W with it CLEAR -- the decline tests neither width within the narrow class nor direction) -- the two
 439:   latch-SET 1R cells cost no session, the six latch-CLEAR cells one each: filed, not owed; and a refusal at
 440:   INTSTAT/INTMASK while the interrupt line is ALREADY asserted (no REFUSAL row here watches the line fall;
 441:   `istw mid'/`p istw mid' watch an ACCEPTED INTMASK store lower it).  The flagship's adjudication, which closes the
 442:   chain: repair16_f2_20260926/fable5_f2_adjudication.md. ***
 443: 
 444: DISCLOSED, not rowed:
 445:   * `goto crime_declined' -> `return 1' is EQUIVALENT on every channel: memory_rw pre-zeroes a device read buffer
 446:     (#95, src/cpus/memory_rw.c -- `if (writeflag == MEM_READ)' then `memset(data, 0, len);', immediately above
 447:     `paddr -= mem->devices[i].baseaddr;'), and on a declined access nothing between the entry and the tail writes
 448:     HARDINT or SOFTINT, so the tail's restore and recompute are identities.  Measured 40/40 (the then 40-row test) in kill table 1.
 449:   * a fall-through confined to the THREE label cells whose arms have NO body for that access, all EQUIVALENT:
 450:       CRIME_DOG (0x30)          `No warning.' -- the arm is `break;'
 451:       CRIME_CONTROL, reads      the arm acts only on MEM_WRITE
 452:       CRIME_REV, outside the PROM-probe window   the arm acts only when the pc is in the window
 453:     The first two measured as survivors in kill table 2 (`!= CRIME_DOG', the CONTROL-read-only fall-through); the REV
 454:     cell is the `lb/lh rev pc' rows' converse, read from the arm.  [This said "the two label cells" until repair 12 --
 455:     kimi CLI, closing pass 6.]
 456:   * ACCEPT cells at unrowed slots: the rows touch accepted accesses at +0x00, +0x04, +0x08, +0x10, +0x18, +0x30,
 457:     +0x34, +0x38, +0x40, +0x210, +0x214, +0x1f8 and +0x278 (not an exhaustive list of what the window accepts); an
 458:     accept arm narrowed by an address strictly INSIDE the window at an unrowed slot (e.g. `len == 8 && relative_addr !=
 459:     0x100', kill table 2's acc8mid, 71/71 on the 71-row test) is not seen.  TOUCHING a slot in ACCEPTS pins its LATCH
 460:     behaviour, never its acceptance -- what pins acceptance is item 6 (`latch said' for the announced form, the value
 461:     rows for the silent form).  [This bullet implied a touched slot was pinned until repair 12 -- the Opus seat, closing
 462:     pass 6.]
 463:   * an effect ADDED to the decline arm and keyed on ONE UNNAMED offset (item 9 rows the READ answer at every named
 464:     label) -- a refused store that lands only at
 465:     +0x31, a declined read answering nonzero only at +0x20, a silent decline only at +0x100, a fall-through only at
 466:     +0x40 (kimi CLI, glm, F2).  The rows pin the refusal floor at every observable LABEL and at eight default-arm
 467:     offsets; the keeps rows catch a landing at CRIME_DOG, INTMASK, the far block and the middle block.  An effect
 468:     keyed on a single ADDRESS BIT is NOT in this class: every bit 0-9 is carried both ways by a refused access of each
 469:     kind that can carry it (the mid session sets bits 0-8, the far block bit 9; an aligned 2-byte access never sets
 470:     bit 0; kimi-k3:cloud, second closing pass, found bits 7 and 8 carried by no refusal at all; codex and the Opus seat,
 471:     fourth closing pass, found 2W LANDING at bit 1 set carried by no read-back store -- now +0x42, `lo keeps').  Note
 472:     `relative_addr / 8': a refused halfword at +0x1e would land on INTMASK's slot, not at +0x1e; the 2W session's
 473:     +0x1e store is not read back, and the INTMASK landing is carried by `imask keeps'.  A landing at
 474:     CRIME_SOFTINT (0x20, not a switch label) is in this class (deepseek, third closing pass).  ONE NAMED CELL IS
 475:     OPEN AND SAID SO (kimi-k3:cloud, closing pass): a refused sb/sh that LANDS only at CRIME_TIME stores <= 0xffff,
 476:     which the time rows' 0.1 s threshold cannot tell from the small multiple of 66 (possibly 0) the first tick adds
 477:     -- clause (e) debt (this said "the 66-990" until GPT-6 Astra's r17 audit).  At INTSTAT
 478:     (the tail recomputes it), CONTROL and REV (the prelude rewrites them) such a landing is EQUIVALENT.
 479:   * a ROUND TRIP cannot observe an accepted WRITE at +0x00 or +0x08 (the prelude rewrites CRIME_REV and CRIME_CONTROL
 480:     on every access) -- but the write's EFFECTS can, and are rowed: from the PROM-probe window an accepted write
 481:     REDIRECTS the pc (revP sw pc, revP sd pc), and at CONTROL the arm's effects (sw08 halts, sw08 msg ctl at 4 bytes;
 482:     acc ctl sd at 8).  [This bullet said "no round trip there can observe whether the store was accepted" as though
 483:     nothing could, and it was wrong twice: the window redirect (measured by the Opus seat, G4) and the 8-byte CONTROL
 484:     write, which no row carried until repair 12 -- closing pass 6.]  The 4R-high cell at +0x00 is carried by `rev pc
 485:     ctl' (its redirect needs the access ACCEPTED), not by `devsig hi', whose 0 a refused read also returns.
 486:   * `odata = idata' in the decline arm: EQUIVALENT by construction -- `idata' is set only under MEM_WRITE and `odata' is
 487:     consumed only under MEM_READ (measured 141/141 on the 141-row test by the Opus seat, closing pass 6).  `cpu->is_32bit' (the REV arm's
 488:     pc-pointer refresh) holds one value per machine, like the configuration lvalues above.  Accepted-side address bits 7
 489:     and 8: the mid session's accepted sd +0x1f8 carries both, before and between its refusals (a latch keyed on them is
 490:     killed -- kimi-k3's C3, 139/141 on the 141-row test); an ACCEPT arm keyed on them is the unrowed-slot class above.
 491:   * ACCEPTS has 46 ENTRIES, not 46 kinds: the 40-cell pre-set/re-arm floor, the two ENDIANESS strengthenings, and four
 492:     positional repeats of default-arm kinds (`sw/lw 0x04' repeat 0x34's low lane; `sd/ld 0x278' repeat 0x40's 8-byte
 493:     kinds, and are the prologue's only accepted access with address bit 9 set -- an unrecorded strengthening until
 494:     repair 12; kimi CLI, closing pass 6).
 495:   * a decline answering a selection of the register's bytes at CRIME_REV, CRIME_CONTROL or CRIME_TIME CONFINED to
 496:     bytes the model holds at 0 there -- REV = 0x11: bytes 1-7; CONTROL = 0x100: byte 0 and bytes 2-7; TIME: the 4-byte
 497:     half above the low word -- is EQUIVALENT (the prelude rewrites REV and CONTROL on every access) -- at TIME only
 498:     WHILE ITS UPPER WORD IS ZERO: the clock update truncates TIME to 32 bits only inside `if (to_add >= 1)', and an
 499:     accepted 8-byte or upper-half write can fill the upper word, so a nonzero upper word survives a zero-delta update
 500:     (a source reading, GPT-6 Astra's r17 audit; this said "TIME is kept to 32 bits" unconditionally, and "no row seeds
 501:     TIME's upper word" until r21 -- the gapped write sessions DO seed it: they plant an `sw' of t0=0x0a0b0c0d at
 502:     TIME, which the 4-byte arm stores in the UPPER word; the update may truncate it at once, and those rows do not
 503:     establish a persistent nonzero upper word at a refused-read observation -- the grok seat's reading of the final
 504:     packet, confirmed by GPT-6 Astra, 2026-09-30).  [Corrected 2026-09-14 from closing pass 5 (glm): this read "the ADDRESSED lanes (bytes 0-1 at a label)",
 505:     which at REV and CONTROL include a NONZERO byte -- item 9's v0 rows exist to catch exactly that selection.]  At
 506:     INTSTAT, INTMASK and DOG every byte is seeded nonzero, so any selection that reaches the bytes a refused lb/lh
 507:     returns shows (Opus, second closing pass; glm, third) -- one confined above them, `& 0xffff0000', is item 9's
 508:     disclosed equivalent (the qualifier: GPT-6 Astra's r17 audit; this said "any selection shows").
 509:   * a latch keyed on a JOINT predicate (e.g. only 2-byte refusals at CRIME_TIME), or on one unnamed offset other than the
 510:     default-arm cells the latch rows refuse at: clause (e), the single-axis generating set being the floor.
 511:   * (closing pass 5; the Opus seat measured each at 141/141 on the 141-row test; the flagship ruling graded each clause
 512:     (e)) a latch re-armed or pre-set by a CONTROL write's ENDIANESS bit (0x100) -- the arm clears it unconditionally and
 513:     never branches on it; the two ENDIANESS writes in ACCEPTS since repair 11 are a strengthening, not a floor claim
 514:     over value bits; the announce CHANNEL keyed on a JOINT of axes (e.g. `(relative_addr == CRIME_INTSTAT && len == 2 ?
 515:     debug : fatal)(') -- item 5 rows the channel on each SINGLE axis; and a decline answering a MACHINE-CONFIGURATION
 516:     lvalue (`d->use_fb', `flag_for_128MB'), which holds one value per machine and is 0 on this probe's -M 64 non-graphics
 517:     ip32 -- a graphics O2 (use_fb = 1) would see `odata = d->use_fb' answer 1.  Unrowable on one machine, like the
 518:     function-static latch below.
 519:   * a re-arm or pre-set inside the HARD_RESET branch of the CONTROL arm: an accepted write that takes it stops every
 520:     CPU, so nothing can follow it in the session.  Unrowable, not merely unrowed.
 521:   * a fall-through only at CRIME_SOFTINT (0x20), which the switch does not name -- measured 71/71 (the 71-row test) by the Opus seat
 522:     (F2, `sft'); it is the single-unnamed-offset class of the bullet above.
 523:   * a FUNCTION-STATIC latch in place of `d->warned' is NOT equivalent in general -- two IP32 machines in one gxemul
 524:     process would share it -- and this single-machine probe cannot see it (kimi-k3:cloud, F2; the pass-2 Opus seat had
 525:     recorded it "equivalent", which holds only for one machine per process).
 526:   * widths 3, 5, 6, 7 -- unreachable CONDITIONALLY: a MIPS load or store issues only 1, 2, 4 and 8, and memory_rw's
 527:     clamp of an access straddling a device's end (`len = mem->devices[i].length - paddr;') cannot make one here only
 528:     because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8 -- one `#define' away from false (filed: `crimesplitwidth').
 529:     The unaligned-pair instructions (lwl/lwr/swl/swr, ldl/ldr) are not rowed.  The RAM-size checks ABOVE the width
 530:     arm (`-M 48' exits at the first CRIME access) are filed, not here.
 531:   * a TRANSLATION of the register decode -- every access landing some whole number of registers away, +1, +2 or
 532:     more, either direction: no table built one, so none is a measured claim here.  The ANCHORED rows (`top8 anchor',
 533:     `top4 anchor': a value the prelude writes by bank index, not through the decode under test) are placed to see
 534:     one; that is a reading, not a measurement (clause (f); the 09-25 re-ruling, as GPT-6 Astra confirmed it).
 535:   * independence between two CRIME instances (the latch is per instance by construction; IP32 has one CRIME).
 536:   * bits the CONTROL arm does not individually test or clear (SOFT_RESET 0x0400, the SYSADC bits, the low nibbles --
 537:     it tests only their aggregate residue against zero): an edit keyed on one is outside this contract because the
 538:     arm does not distinguish them (clause (e); repair 16's F2
 539:     adjudication, X7).  Accepted rows write only bit 0 of them -- ACCEPTS' 0x0001 and 0x0201, both widths, both latch
 540:     states (opus_r15p2_20260926/accepts_ctl_writes.out); this said "written by no accepted row" until GPT-6 Astra's
 541:     r17 audit.
 542: 
 543: Sentinel: CRIMEP_DONE (plus CRIMEP_RESULT=n/N and CRIMEP_CONTROL=OK|FAIL).
 544: """
 545: import os, pty, re, select, signal, sys, time
 546: 
 547: BIN = sys.argv[1]
 548: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"
 549: DUMMY = "/tmp/dummy_crimep.bin"
 550: if not os.path.exists(DUMMY):
 551:     with open(DUMMY, "wb") as f:
 552:         f.write(b"\0" * 16)
 553: 
 554: CODE = 0x80001000
 555: SCRATCH_RAM = 0xa0001800
 950:     "CONTROL: two MACE stores latch HARDINT (raw %s)" % hint)
 951: row("gate line", ip2(nth(t, "cause", 0)), "set", "CONTROL: the CRIME line is asserted")
 952: row("gate run", pr(t, "v1"), "0x%x" % LIVE_VAL, "refused sh 0x800 +0x08 with an irq latched: CPUs run")
 953: row("gate lb v0", pr(t, "t1"), "0x0", "refused lb +0x08 with HARDINT nonzero answers 0")
 954: row("gate lh v0", pr(t, "s3"), "0x0", "refused lh +0x08 with HARDINT nonzero answers 0")
 955: 
 956: # ---- the TIME label: an accepted read returns the value of the PREVIOUS update, then updates -- so a refused access
 957: #  that reached crime_update_crime_time() would show in the NEXT read.  The first `ld' latches last_microseconds; on the
 958: #  fixed build the only other update before the next `ld' is the device tick's FIRST firing -- ticks_till_next starts at
 959: #  0, so it fires right after the session's first `ld' (the Opus closing seat; this said "nothing else updates TIME"
 960: #  until then), and it adds the few microseconds since the latch: the small multiple of 66 (possibly 0) the rows print -- this said "the 66-990" until r21 -- (measured across 52 cells
 961: #  against SMALL = 6.6e6).  Later ticks are 2^14 cycles apart and a session steps a few dozen instructions; a fall-through at 0x38
 962: #  makes it the wall-clock interval of the intervening debugger commands, ~1e8.  The third `ld' is the CONTROL that the
 963: #  channel moves.  (Opus pass 2, E3; the tick-spacing wording corrected by the kimi CLI seat on the F2 pass.)
 964: #  ASSUMPTION, disclosed: after that FIRST tick, no further tick falls between the first `ld' and the `ld' that samples
 965: #  s1 (codex, closing pass: the window runs THROUGH the sampling read, not only to the refused access; deepseek and
 966: #  codex, second closing pass: this sentence said "no tick boundary" while the one above names the first tick).  The IRQ rows carry the same assumption:
 967: #  dev_crime_tick also calls crime_interrupt_reassert(), so a tick inside a session could raise IP2 on the fixed build
 968: #  (kimi CLI, closing pass) -- a false red, never a false green; measured stable so far.
 969: SMALL = 66 * 100000
 970: 
 971: 
 972: def mag(v):
 973:     return "absent" if v is None else ("small" if v < SMALL else "large")
 974: 
 975: 
 976: for op in ("lb", "sb", "lh", "sh"):
 977:     A = Addr(CODE)
 978:     c = []
 979:     x, _ = ld(A, "ld", CRIME + 0x38, "s0"); c += x
 980:     if op in ("lb", "lh"):
 981:         x, _ = ld(A, op, CRIME + 0x38, "v0"); c += x
 982:     else:
 983:         x, _ = st(A, op, CRIME + 0x38, 0xff if op == "sb" else 0xffff); c += x
 984:     x, _ = ld(A, "ld", CRIME + 0x38, "s1"); c += x
 985:     x, _ = ld(A, "ld", CRIME + 0x38, "s2"); c += x
 986:     if op == "lb":                                  # a second refusal: the TIME-first latch cell
 987:         x, _ = ld(A, "lb", CRIME + 0x07, "v1"); c += x
 988:     t, clean = session(c + ["print s1", "print s2", "print v0"])
 989:     s1, s2 = nth(t, "s1", 0), nth(t, "s2", 0)
 990:     row("time %s" % op, mag(s1), "small", "after refused %s +0x38 (raw %s)" % (op, s1))
 991:     row("time %s ctl" % op, mag(s2), "large", "CONTROL: accepted ld moved TIME (raw %s)" % s2)
 992:     if op in ("lb", "lh"):
 993:         row("time %s v0" % op, pr(t, "v0"), "0x0", "refused %s +0x38 answers 0" % op)
 994:     if op == "lb":
 995:         row("time once", count(t, "-- declined.", clean), 1, "first refusal at CRIME_TIME, then +0x07: one notice")
1643: row("p istw sd", ip2(nth(t, "cause", 1)), "set", "POST: accepted sd +0x10 reasserts")
1644: row("p istw mid", ip2(nth(t, "cause", 2)), "clear", "CONTROL: lowered again")
1645: row("p istw sw", ip2(nth(t, "cause", 3)), "set", "POST: accepted sw +0x10 reasserts")
1646: 
1647: # ---- P4/P5: THE TIME 4-BYTE CELLS, POST, IN THE **GAPPED** SHAPE.  *** THE TWO OBVIOUS SHAPES
1648: #      WERE MEASURED VACUOUS (post7b.py) and one gave a FALSE RED on a control; only this one
1649: #      discriminates, at ~13,000x (base 0x13414f8 vs the bypass's 0x5ee). ***  The gap is the
1650: #      debugger's own pause BETWEEN steps: host time passes, so an update that is performed
1651: #      arrives before the final 8R and one that is skipped arrives after it.  CHANNEL: a read
1652: #      takes odata BEFORE its own crime_update_crime_time(). ----
1653: def gapped_post(kind):
1654:     ops = [enc("lb", "a3", "t1"),                                            # REFUSED lb -- sets the latch
1655:            enc("ld", "at", "v1"),                                            # TIME 8R, TIME still ~0
1656:            enc("sw", "at", "t0") if kind == "w" else enc("lw", "at", "a0"),  # the cell under test
1657:            enc("ld", "at", "v0")]                                            # what it left behind
1658:     c = ["at=0x%x" % (CRIME + 0x38), "a3=0x%x" % (CRIME + 0x07), "t0=0x0a0b0c0d",
1659:          "v0=0x%x" % SENT, "v1=0x%x" % SENT, "a0=0x%x" % SENT, "t1=0x%x" % SENT]
1660:     for i, op in enumerate(ops):
