 161: ### `crimectllane` (HIGH, device) - CRIME_CONTROL acts on the raw value of whatever width reaches the exact label 0x08
 162: 
 163: `dev_sgi_ip32.c`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(crime)`, `case CRIME_CONTROL:` (0x008) matches the EXACT label and acts on the RAW
 164: `idata` of the access that reached it.  So a 32-bit `sw 0x800` to `+0x08` -- the HIGH half of the 64-bit register on this
 165: big-endian machine -- carries bit 11 into `CRIME_CONTROL_HARD_RESET` and stops every CPU, while a 32-bit write to
 166: `+0x0c`, the lane that holds bit 11 and the offset NetBSD 1.6.2 writes (the arm's own TODO says so), performs the
 167: register store and reaches the default arm's log, bypassing CONTROL's reset and watchdog handling.  MEASURED by `#529`'s
 168: pass-1 Opus seat (`crimewidthkill/opus_pass1_20260913/out/rows_base.out`: `sw CTL+08 0x800` halted; `sw CTL+0c 0x800`
 169: did not halt, `dflt=1`).  (A draft of this entry said the `+0x0c` write "does nothing" -- GPT-6 Astra's records audit.)  `#529`'s detector USES this defect as a channel
 170: (`sw08 halts`, `sw08 msg ctl`, the `sh08` rows) and says so; a round that fixes the lane owes those rows' re-derivation.
 171: Needs a guest witness of what a real driver writes (the PROM's reboot path; NetBSD's watchdog) before choosing a lane
 172: model.  **A probe comment and `gate_arm.sh` have called this row "filed" since 2026-09-13 (a second probe comment called
 173: `crimebankorder` filed); the resumption dossier found neither filing, and the flagship's 09-25 re-ruling listed both.**  **Graded HIGH, not MED:** stopping
 174: every CPU ends the emulation in ordinary single-machine execution without `debugger_enter_at_end_of_run` (`emul.c`
 175: enters the debugger instead when it is set) and the process returns, so a guest store that on the header's
 176: model reaches only reserved high-word bits ends the emulator -- the severity rule's HIGH.  GPT-6 Astra's confirmation of
 177: the codex farm's adjudication (`codexfarm_20260926/adjudication/codex_astraconfirm_farm_f1c.txt`) overturned the Fable
 178: seat's MED; that seat's argument -- the guest gains no capability it lacks through the legitimate 64-bit HARD_RESET --
 179: bears on reachability ranking, not on severity.
